Sluice Notes 019

There is no HTML version of this letter and there never will be one; the whole
thing is written in a text editor, sent by a nine-line shell script, and read
by about two hundred people who like it that way.

This week: rope. Specifically, why three-strand hemp is still sold next to
eight-plait polyester, who buys which, and what a chandlery owner in a small
town can tell you about both in under a minute.

Next week: the same shop's opinion on knots, which is stronger than it needs
to be.

